# neos-accessibility — turn on speech when the user chose the Screen Reader
# boot entry.
#
# The GRUB/syslinux "NeOS (Screen Reader)" entry passes `accessibility=on` on
# the kernel command line. On any other boot both modes exit 0 and do nothing.
#
#   neos-accessibility            (root, neos-accessibility.service, before the
#                                  display manager) starts espeakup, so the
#                                  virtual consoles speak, and lets the root
#                                  installer onto the accessibility bus.
#   neos-accessibility --session  (the user's desktop session, from
#                                  /etc/xdg/autostart/neos-screen-reader.desktop)
#                                  turns on Plasma's screen reader and starts
#                                  Orca, so the desktop, the welcome window and
#                                  the apps speak too. espeakup alone left a
#                                  blind user in a silent desktop.
=======
# neos-accessibility — activate screen-reader speech in the live session when
# the user chose the Accessibility boot entry.
#
# The GRUB/syslinux accessibility menu entry passes `accessibility=on` on the
# kernel command line.  When present, this script starts espeakup so blind
# users hear speech output on the virtual console immediately after login.
# On a normal (non-accessibility) boot the script exits 0 and does nothing.
